><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Cis Regulation by Riboswitches</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="534" name="Google Shape;534;p73"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr><p:ph idx="1" type="body"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="228600" y="1371600"/><a:ext cx="4876800" cy="4191000"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr anchorCtr="0" anchor="t" bIns="45700" lIns="91425" spcFirstLastPara="1" rIns="91425" wrap="square" tIns="45700"><a:noAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2800"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="1" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Riboswitch </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>= domain of an mRNA that can </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="0000FF"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>bind a small-molecule ligand</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="560"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2800"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>The binding of ligand affects conformation of the mRNA and its activity.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="560"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2800"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Thus, riboswitches allow mRNA to participate in their own regulation and </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="0000FF"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>respond to changing concentrations of the ligand</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="535" name="Google Shape;535;p73"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="280987" y="990600"/><a:ext cx="8458200" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="A three-part diagram illustrating the regulation of bacterial mRNA function in cis by riboswitches. From the top, a green hammer-like structure with its head facing left has two large circles at the head, and middle, and two smaller circles toward the end of the handle on the right. The middle large circle is labeled Aptamer. The first large circle has two lines sitting on top of it and below it. The entire structure is lined, with the exception of the circles. The second circle connects down to a green line of the same color. From the left, the line is labeled 5’ and extends up and right, and then on the right side of the bottom of the structure that connects up to the circle, the line starts again and extends right; at its end is a 3’. Slightly to the right on the line is a red section, labeled as ribosome-bonding site. Below this is an arrow pointing down that has a curved arrow entering it from the right. Next to the arrow on the right is a green oval, labeled TPP. This points down to structure a, which shows a similar structure as described, but the Aptamer has engulfed the TPP, and the left side of the hammer head closes in on the TPP on the left. One of the smaller circles creates an extension to the right; this is labeled poly(U) terminator. To the right is a gray text box, which reads “Stabilization of a transcription terminator structure aborts transcription.” Part b is a similar structure, but this time the poly (U) terminator curves up and left, and then extends right. The gray text box to the right reads, “Blockage of the ribosome-binding site blocks translation.” Part c also shows a similar structure as part a, but the 5’ end of the green line is chopped off, with the letters GUACGG to the right; this is labeled as 5’ splice site. Above this is the rest of the image, and to the right of the structure is the rest of the line. About half way to the right, the letters, “AG” are shown and labeled, 3’ splice site. To the right of AG is the rest of the green line. The gray text box on the right reads, “Regulation of intron splicing in fungal and plant introns.”" id="536" name="Google Shape;536;p73"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="5105400" y="1219200"/><a:ext cx="3848100" cy="5476875"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>